{name:OY,description:`Runs a shell command and returns its output.
- Always set the \`workdir\` param when using the shell_command function. Do not use \`cd\` unless absolutely necessary. For doing file changes, use the ${qD}
- Avoid end-buffering pipes like \`| tail -20\` for long-running commands; they can hide progress and trigger inactivity timeouts
- Use \`timeout_ms\` to increase the inactivity timeout for commands that may stay quiet for long stretches`,inputSchema:{type:"object",properties:{command:{type:"string",description:"Shell command to execute."},workdir:{type:"string",description:"Optional working directory to run the command in; defaults to the turn cwd."},login:{type:"boolean",description:"Whether to run the shell with login shell semantics. Defaults to true."},timeout_ms:{type:"number",description:"The timeout for the command in milliseconds"}},required:["command"],additionalProperties:!1},source:"builtin",meta:{disableTimeout:!0},executionProfile:{serial:!1,resourceKeys:()=>[]}}

